<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Molecular Modeling | Yassir Boulaamane</title><link>https://yboulaamane.github.io/tags/molecular-modeling/</link><atom:link href="https://yboulaamane.github.io/tags/molecular-modeling/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>Molecular Modeling</description><generator>Hugo Blox Builder (https://hugoblox.com)</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>https://yboulaamane.github.io/media/icon_hu_4d696a8ace2a642b.png</url><title>Molecular Modeling</title><link>https://yboulaamane.github.io/tags/molecular-modeling/</link></image><item><title>Beyond 2D Fingerprints: Encoding Protein-Ligand Interactions for Machine Learning</title><link>https://yboulaamane.github.io/blog/beyond-2d-fingerprints-3d-protein-ligand-interaction-encoding-for-ml/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://yboulaamane.github.io/blog/beyond-2d-fingerprints-3d-protein-ligand-interaction-encoding-for-ml/</guid><description>&lt;p>A 2D fingerprint throws away the pose. Docking spent its time on contacts, hydrogen-bond geometry, and stacking, and a topology-only vector keeps none of that. Use a 2D fingerprint when the ligand alone is the object. Use a 3D interaction fingerprint when the pose is the object.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>PLEC, SPLIF, and E3FP are three different objects. PLEC encodes which groups touch. SPLIF encodes the geometry of those contacts. E3FP never sees the protein.&lt;/p>
&lt;figure style="margin:2rem 0;">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 640 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="fp3d-title fp3d-desc" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
&lt;title id="fp3d-title">Three fingerprints, three questions&lt;/title>
&lt;desc id="fp3d-desc">PLEC encodes contact chemistry between protein and ligand. SPLIF encodes the spatial geometry of interacting fragments. E3FP encodes ligand shape and pharmacophore and does not see the protein.&lt;/desc>
&lt;g fill="none" stroke-width="2">
&lt;rect x="24" y="72" width="188" height="160" rx="14" fill="#2f80ed" fill-opacity="0.10" stroke="#2f80ed"/>
&lt;rect x="226" y="72" width="188" height="160" rx="14" fill="#9b51e0" fill-opacity="0.10" stroke="#9b51e0"/>
&lt;rect x="428" y="72" width="188" height="160" rx="14" fill="#f2994a" fill-opacity="0.10" stroke="#f2994a"/>
&lt;/g>
&lt;g fill="currentColor" font-family="system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif" text-anchor="middle">
&lt;text x="320" y="40" font-size="22" font-weight="700">Match the fingerprint to the question&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="118" y="112" font-size="18" font-weight="700">PLEC&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="118" y="142" font-size="16">Who touches whom&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="118" y="170" font-size="15">Protein and ligand&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="118" y="198" font-size="15">Affinity, reactivity&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="320" y="112" font-size="18" font-weight="700">SPLIF&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="320" y="142" font-size="16">How they sit&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="320" y="170" font-size="15">Protein and ligand&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="320" y="198" font-size="15">Pose vs a reference&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="522" y="112" font-size="18" font-weight="700">E3FP&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="522" y="142" font-size="16">Ligand shape&lt;/text>
&lt;text x="522" y="170" font-size="15">Ligand only&lt;/text>
